            <title>[LU-21113] sanity-sec test_81b: Can not get multiop_pid, ZFS OSS write RPC stalled 63s in txg_wait_synced</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21113</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_81b fails with "Can not get multiop_pid from /tmp/multiop_bg.pid.N" when an OSS on ZFS stalls a write RPC for over 60 seconds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on lustre-reviews review-dne-zfs-part-2 (RHEL 9.8 client/servers, 4 MDT, 8 OST on ZFS), change 64875 patchset 37 (unrelated to the failing test), session 6188c4e6-7a5b-49ed-a8df-445609cee64d, subtest efab28b7-1dca-4418-98c0-7dbc29ede219.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test writes 3 bytes to a file with echo, then starts multiop (OP1024yY_c) on the same client, which writes 1024 bytes and calls fsync before it writes its pid file. rmultiop_start waits 60 seconds for the pid file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client debug log: the second ll_write_begin blocks from 1793687325.63 until 1793687377.79, when the earlier dirty extent on OST0004 finishes; the fsync and its brw RPC then complete in under 1 ms. The OSC imports had gone IDLE after 21s in between and reconnected, but the connects were fine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OSS dmesg (onyx-144vm13): "ll_ost_io00_012: service thread pid 538611 was inactive for 40.388 seconds", stack in ofd_commitrw_write -&amp;gt; ofd_write_attr_set -&amp;gt; osd_trans_stop -&amp;gt; txg_wait_synced, then "completed after 63.341s". The RPC is logged as processed in 63341377us. So the write RPC waited over 60 s for a ZFS txg sync, longer than rmultiop_start's 60 s limit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No earlier failure with this error in 730 days. The test has other failures (mkdir failed, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18461" title="Lustre join file re-implementation" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18461"&gt;LU-18461&lt;/a&gt;) that are a different cause. Possible fixes: have rmultiop_start wait longer in test_81b, or find why the txg sync stalled on the ZFS OSS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-64875-ps37-03d3af31542c on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/64875" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/64875&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
